# Unreleased
  - Compose KV, List, Set and BTree APIs around shared routing and request execution.
  - Separate command construction and response parsing from node transport lifetime.
  - Exchange immutable command requests through a narrow submit interface.
  - Separate ZooKeeper discovery, consistent hash ring and locator lifecycle.
  - Return complete node statistics and correct Set drop/pipe command construction.
  - Recognize successful collection deletion with DELETED_DROPPED.
  - Package the core client for Python 3.11+ with pyproject.toml.
  - Separate client, routing, encoding, results and protocol classes under src/arcus.
  - Preserve existing imports and move administration utilities under tools/.
  - Standardize Python formatting and add independent regression tests.
  - Fix asynchronous result deadlines, repeated reads, and concurrent waiters.
  - Report invalidated operations as connection errors rather than cache misses.
  - Detect socket EOF and reject malformed get/gets responses.
  - Correct CAS arguments and BTree decrement dispatch.
  - Skip invalidated queued requests to preserve response ordering.
  - Bound connection, I/O and submitted operation waits with configurable timeouts.
  - Release node, worker, epoll and ZooKeeper resources on shutdown and failed setup.
  - Preserve signed integers and dates before the Unix epoch when decoding values.
  - Refresh ZooKeeper membership without blocking cache routing and bound initial reads.
  - Add isolated Linux integration tests and Python package CI checks.
  - Add reproducible client benchmarks and isolated fault/resource experiments.

